  "interpretation": [
    "Without any browser request interception, Chromium and Firefox complete eight journeys at both mounts. Firefox receives two actual 404s for the selected module, then one 200 after restoration.",
    "WebKit fails the same recovery on both mounts: one real module 404, zero early 200s, zero restored 200s; both link navigation and explicit reload fail. This rules out request interception as a necessary trigger in this environment.",
    "Actual Rust restarts load the deliberately incomplete manifest then the exact original manifest. Session and bucket rows including xmin remain unchanged. Missing responses carry no-store.",
    "The pattern matches WebKit bug 270357: speculative modulepreload failure can persist in memory across reload. This source-based explanation is an inference consistent with the actual observations; no WebKit internal trace was taken."
  ],
